WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.244
Energy-smart workflows make important work less dependent on perfect willpower.

2
00:00:05.244 --> 00:00:08.541
Time blocking by energy level is one practical move.

3
00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:16.257
Put deep work, difficult decisions, learning, and creative problem solving into better capacity windows when possible.

4
00:00:16.257 --> 00:00:19.554
Put lower-intensity administration into batches.

5
00:00:19.554 --> 00:00:26.521
This reduces the number of times attention has to shift and helps protect the kind of energy each task requires.

6
00:00:26.521 --> 00:00:29.293
Meeting hygiene is part of workflow design.

7
00:00:29.293 --> 00:00:35.436
Meetings should have a purpose, the right participants, a realistic scope, and a useful outcome.

8
00:00:35.436 --> 00:00:40.306
Decision batching can reduce the number of scattered choices across the day.

9
00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.977
Checklists can lower cognitive load for recurring tasks.

10
00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:51.094
Templates and defaults reduce startup cost because people do not have to recreate the same structure every time.

11
00:00:51.094 --> 00:00:53.417
Shutdown routines help close loops.

12
00:00:53.417 --> 00:01:03.231
A useful shutdown can capture unfinished work, identify the next action, record decisions, and clear enough mental space to stop carrying the day forward.

13
00:01:03.231 --> 00:01:05.928
This is not about forcing longer workdays.

14
00:01:05.928 --> 00:01:12.221
It is about making the next start easier and reducing the background hum of unresolved commitments.

15
00:01:12.221 --> 00:01:14.919
A clean stop often creates a cleaner start.

16
00:01:14.919 --> 00:01:17.016
Distraction design matters too.

17
00:01:17.016 --> 00:01:21.736
Create friction for distractions and reduce friction for important work.

18
00:01:21.736 --> 00:01:32.375
That might mean turning off nonessential alerts during focus blocks, keeping key materials ready, using a visible task limit, or setting a default place for decisions.

19
00:01:32.375 --> 00:01:35.596
The best workflow is not the most elaborate system.

20
00:01:35.596 --> 00:01:40.765
It is the system that quietly makes the right action easier under real conditions.
